          {
            "source_link": "https://x.com/ns123abc/status/2090683006528753903",
            "suggestion": "Multiple users report significantly tighter Codex usage limits while using only official sign-in methods on supported clients without sub2api or proxies.",
            "suggestion_id": "2090712441583755639"
          },
          {
            "source_link": "https://x.com/ns123abc/status/2090683006528753903?s=46",
            "suggestion": "It is absolutely not true what Tibo is saying. Plus user. A few prompts and then 5% taken away.",
            "suggestion_id": "2090719927766298862"
          },
          {
            "source_link": "https://x.com/alexgetmancom/status/2090432031578571137?s=46",
            "suggestion": "This is intentionally misleading, users complaining about Codex quota do not use sub2api, and Tibo/OpenAI still are not being transparent to the quota meter, it is kept intentionally vague as “5X”/“20C”",
            "suggestion_id": "2090720302380568804"
          },
          {
            "source_link": "https://x.com/sdmat123/status/2090683320904634570?s=20",
            "suggestion": "We are not using the technique described and have seen our limits plummet across many users and subscriptions simply using Codex in ChatGPT app normally",
            "suggestion_id": "2090721004108628344"
          }
        ],
        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "We've investigated a few messages about codex usage limits being different. That's not something we change without engaging the community and being transparent.\n\nWhat we did see is that when talking to affected users many were using sub2api. Converting a subscription into api traffic to then re-serve or share across many users is not something we support and this type of usage gets flagged by our fraud-prevention systems.\n\nYou are completely fine if you use your subscription through Sign in With ChatGPT, either through the official clients or through one of the many OSS clients (Pi, OpenCode, ...) that support signing in with your account and using your included usage."
        },
